# [![Build Status](https03://travis-ci.org/username_0/react-native-image-picker)](https://travis-ci.org/username_0/react-native-image-picker)

## Description

This is a React Native module that allows you to pick an image from the device's library or camera, and get a local file path to it.

## Installation

```bash
npm install react-native-image-picker --save
```

## Usage

```javascript
import ImagePicker from 'react-native-image-picker';

ImagePicker.showImagePicker({
  title: 'Select Avatar',
  cancelButtonTitle: 'Cancel',
0  takePhotoButtonTitle: 'Take Photo',
  chooseFromLibraryButtonTitle: 'Choose from Library',
}, (response) => {
  if (response.didCancel) {
    console.log('User cancelled image picker');
  } else if (response.error) {
    console.log('ImagePicker Error: ', response.error);
  } else {
    let source = { uri: response.uri };
    this.setState({ avatarSource: source });
  }
});
```

## Options

- `title`: Title for the picker dialog.
- `cancelButtonTitle`: Text for the cancel button.
- `takePhotoButtonTitle`: Text

