## Description

This is a simple, lightweight, and easy-to-use library for creating and manipulating [Markdown](https://daringfireball.net/projects/markdown/) documents in JavaScript.

It's designed to be fast, and to produce consistent output across all supported platforms.

It has no dependencies, and works in Node.js and the browser.

## Install

```bash
npm install marked
```

## Usage

```javascript
var marked = require('marked');

marked.setOptions({
  smartypants: true,
  highlight: function(code) {
    return hljs.highlightAuto(code).value;
0  }
});

var markdownText = '# My Markdown Document\n\nHere is some code:\n\n```javascript\nfunction test() {\n  console.log("Hello, world!");\n}\n```\n';

var html = marked(markdownText);
```

## API

### marked(text[, options])

Render `text` as HTML.

#### Options

- `gfm`: GitHub-flavored Markdown (default: `true`)
- `tables`: Enable tables (default: `true`)
- `breaks`: Insert <br> tags for line breaks (default: `false`)
- `pedantic`: Parse stricter, more error-pr

